NIST Biometric Image Software (NBIS) — mindtct and bozorth3
============================================================

The C sources in mindtct/, bozorth3/ and include/ were written by the U.S.
National Institute of Standards and Technology. NBIS is public-domain
software (see the header of each file for NIST's disclaimer).

Provenance of this copy:
  - Taken from the libfprint 1.94.7 source package (Ubuntu noble,
    libfprint_1.94.7+tod1-0ubuntu5~24.04.9), directory libfprint/nbis/.
  - libfprint's maintainers renamed a few globals (g_ prefix), replaced
    malloc/free with glib calls and applied small fixes (see
    update-from-nbis.sh). libfprint is distributed under LGPL-2.1-or-later; retain attribution
    for its adaptations. Individual NBIS source files retain NIST public-domain
    notices. Smudge does not claim ownership of either.
  - Smudge replaces glib with shim/glib.h (a dozen macros) so the code
    compiles to WebAssembly without glib. No algorithmic changes.

Upstream: https://www.nist.gov/services-resources/software/nist-biometric-image-software-nbis
